  "description" : "The insert - the whole reason risk R-B matters. Everything validates, CONFIRMI holds 'Y', so the EVALUATE at :169 takes the first arm at :171 and performs ADD-TRANSACTION. :444 moves HIGH-VALUES into TRAN-ID, :445-447 position a browse past the end, read the record with the highest key and end the browse, :448 moves that key into WS-TRAN-ID-N PIC 9(16) and :449 adds one - so a master whose highest key is ...0003 yields ...0004. :450 INITIALIZE TRAN-RECORD and :451-467 fill it, including a second FUNCTION NUMVAL-C conversion of TRNAMTI at :456 whose result is stored into TRAN-AMT PIC S9(09)V99 as the zoned image 0000000123D - eleven characters, the trailing digit carrying the positive overpunch. The record written at :713 is the full 350 bytes CVTRA05Y declares, trailing FILLER PIC X(20) included and space filled (gates G19, G21). The write reports NORMAL, so :725 INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS blanks all fifteen receivers before the notice is composed - which is why every input field on the sent screen is blank and the cursor is back on ACTIDINL - :727 moves DFHGREEN into ERRMSGC, and :728-733 STRING two literals, TRAN-ID DELIMITED BY SPACE and a full stop into WS-MESSAGE. The two literals each carry a space at the joining edge, so the notice contains two spaces after 'successfully.'; and a zero-filled sixteen-digit key contains no space, so all sixteen digits appear. TRANSACT is left holding four rows in key sequence.",
